(* S-P1.Q2 — correct model, DEGRADED mode, sole channel compromised.   *)
(* Variant: the P1 [model] binding claim in the hard case.             *)
(*                                                                      *)
(* Registered prediction (PREDICTIONS.md, frozen 5188e7a):             *)
(* (i)  headline AcceptedUnderHonestKey ==> IssuerSigned: unreachable, *)
(*      terminating (p~0.70); real violation (p~0.10) = amendment      *)
(*      trigger on the verifier specification, not a recut; timeout   *)
(*      (p~0.20).                                                      *)
(* (ii) unrestricted AcceptS ==> IssuerSigned: VIOLATION as registered *)
(*      (p~0.85) via impersonation under the adversary's own key;      *)
(*      unexpectedly unreachable (p~0.10) = model defect; timeout 0.05.*)
(* (iii) N1 HonestAccepted reachable. Timebox: 30 min.                 *)
(*                                                                      *)
(* This model proves: in degraded mode with the sole authority channel *)
(* compromised, under an adversary that can alter any bytes after      *)
(* issue, holds every key it uses, and has the A1.3 item 3 (DSKS)      *)
(* capability, framed bytes accepted under an honest issuer's key are  *)
(* exactly the bytes that issuer signed at an issuance event — the     *)
(* [model] binding half of P1 in its §A3.1 operative form, as a        *)
(* non-injective correspondence.                                       *)
(* This model does not prove: the verdict partition (P4, TLA+); that   *)
(* acceptance is fresh or context-bound (replay is permitted, §A3.1    *)
(* item 1); that the accepted key is an honest issuer's (P10 / the     *)
(* first link — in degraded-compromised mode it need not be [CORRECTION 2026-09-12, author C5 read: was "it is not", too strong — honest-key acceptance stays reachable, N1 HonestAccepted .out:396] — and the *)
(* unrestricted contrast query (ii) is registered red); re-attribution *)
(* of honest bytes to another key (S-P3, complementary — composed at   *)
(* the capstone, not consumed here); the multi-signer set (S-P2);      *)
(* canonicalization or the frame's byte layout (P8); wrapper soundness *)
(* (P7); anything temporal (P5/P6); the verification profile (H1a).    *)
(* Composition with a same-key signing endpoint outside this fixture   *)
(* (key-use discipline, CORRECTION item 8 below; RESULTS.md ledger     *)
(* entry 5) is not proved either: the claim is over a CLOSED producer  *)
(* set (reviewer's verdict on this header, 2026-09-06).                *)
(* Load-bearing checks (for the headline): the attestation-signature   *)
(* check `let (=BYTES, =fb) = checksign(sg, kX)` binding the PRESENTED *)
(* bytes to the SIGNED bytes, resting on signature unforgeability      *)
(* (library, Dolev-Yao). Confirmed by the S-P1 probes (RESULTS.md,     *)
(* "Load-bearing / carried, from ablation"): only this check, and the  *)
(* unforgeability of sign, move the headline; independently confirmed  *)
(* by the cross-family review's single-removal matrix (2026-09-06,     *)
(* RECORDED item 4 below): every other check is inert for the          *)
(* headline on its own, which does not license removing several        *)
(* together.                                                           *)
(* Carried checks (not exercised by these queries): the fingerprint    *)
(* match and manifest-hash check (S-P3), possession over the manifest  *)
(* (A1.5/P10, S-P3 entry 2), the authority-evidence check (inert in    *)
(* degraded-compromised mode by construction, S-P3 F6), algorithm      *)
(* identifier (A3 identifier-binding invariant, per F7), issuer        *)
(* identity (S-P3 F8 and its 2026-09-05 ruling). Signed fields carried *)
(* as OBLIGATIONS, not checks: object type (P7) and canonicalization   *)
(* version / algorithm profile (P8/H1a) — ot and cv are bound at the   *)
(* frame pattern and never compared (CORRECTION item 7 below).         *)
(*                                                                      *)
(* Theory: formal/suite/lib/tessera_theory.pvl (D-3 possession over    *)
(* manifest; D-4 DSKS expressible; D-5 object-type constants).          *)
(* First link in the SELECTED form: transcription binding, evidence =  *)
(* sign((STMT_DIGEST, h(t)), skCh); the sole channel's key is public.  *)
(* Frame: framed(objType, alg, issuerId, kfp, mh, canonVer, payload)   *)
(* under BYTES — copied VERBATIM from S-P3 (library header: NOT        *)
(* promoted; shared by copy). Object type is the library's OT_ATTEST.  *)
(* Fixture (PREDICTIONS.md "Fixture statement", N1/N2): TWO honest     *)
(* issuers, each with its own honestly published manifest, replicated  *)
(* with adversary-chosen payloads; N1 witness HonestAccepted emitted   *)
(* by the judge, must be reachable.                                     *)
(* Judge encoding as registered (PREDICTIONS.md "The judge"): judge H  *)
(* keyed on honest KEYS (honestKeyCh), judge N1 keyed on honest        *)
(* (key, bytes) reports; report outputs parallel with continuations   *)
(* (S-P3 recut 1); judge locals never shadow library names.            *)
(*                                                                      *)
(* Run: proverif -lib ../../lib/tessera_theory.pvl sp1_q2_degraded_compromised.pv *)
(*                                                                     *)
(* RECORDED 2026-09-06 (cross-family review item 4): the reviewer's    *)
(* single-removal matrix (docs/reviews/                                *)
(* 2026-09-06-codex-suite-falsification-s-p1-s-p2-s-p7-s-standing.md,  *)
