(* under falsification-2026-09-06/scratch/; RESULT lines reproduced    *)
(* by the collaborator 2026-09-06, RESULTS.md review log) agrees with  *)
(* probes p1-p7: the headline stays true under every single removal    *)
(* except the attestation-signature check (m_G_signature.out:314) and  *)
(* its byte/key equalities (m_G_sig_bytes.out, m_G_sig_key.out per     *)
(* the matrix); the unrestricted (ii) was already red. No header       *)
(* sentence here named an inert check load-bearing; nothing narrowed.  *)
(* CORRECTION 2026-09-06 (cross-family review item 7): "Carried        *)
(* checks" listed "object type (P7); canonicalization version and      *)
(* algorithm profile (P8/H1a)" as checks. There are no such checks:    *)
(* ot and cv are bound by the frame pattern and never compared. The    *)
(* reviewer's A6 adds an honest issuance of a wrapper-typed frame      *)
(* under a foreign version and presents it to this verifier            *)
(* unchanged: accepted (a6_foreign_type.out:747) — unchanged signed-   *)
(* byte replay, not a P1 counterexample. Reworded as signed fields     *)
(* carried as obligations for P7 and P8/H1a.                           *)
(* CORRECTION 2026-09-06 (cross-family review item 8): "This model     *)
(* proves" holds for a CLOSED producer set — every signature under an  *)
(* honest issuer key is made by this model's Issuer, which signs only  *)
(* framed objects under BYTES (and its manifest under POSS). The       *)
(* reviewer's A8 adds a second honest endpoint under the same key      *)
(* that signs a payload-only message; asked to sign an attacker-       *)
(* chosen inner frame as payload, it lets this verifier accept that    *)
(* frame with no matching issuance event: headline false               *)
(* (a8_cross_broken_endpoint.out:428). The added endpoint is broken    *)
(* by construction; this fixture is not falsified. Named assumption,   *)
(* key-use discipline: RESULTS.md ledger entry 5.                      *)
(* RECORDED 2026-09-06 (cross-family review item 11): the reviewer's   *)
(* A5, a judge demanding two identical acceptance reports, returned    *)
(* "cannot be proved" (a5_repeat_replay_uncertain.out:689):            *)
(* inconclusive, neither reachable nor unreachable. Injectivity is     *)
(* not a registered requirement (A3 section A3.1 registers the non-    *)
(* injective form); nothing here claims it.                            *)
(* BOUNDARY 2026-09-06 (cross-family review items 1-3): signature-set  *)
(* operations (A1.3 item 2) are unrepresentable here — one signature   *)
(* slot; the signer set is S-P2's subject. Byte-encoding attacks       *)
(* (non-canonical encodings, hash-input ambiguity, cross-kind parse    *)
(* confusion) are unrepresentable in every family: term equality       *)
(* stands in for byte equality and distinct constructors never         *)
(* confuse — in the reviewer's words, "a coverage failure, not an      *)
(* unreachable attack"; P8's injectivity obligation and the library's  *)
(* h/fp idealization (Layer 2), as the "does not prove" list assigns.  *)
